# Software Development Rules

## Real Methods Policy

**Production code always uses real methods and implementations - no mocks, stubs, or fake methods.**

### Implementation Requirements
- All functions must use real library/tool implementations (weasyprint, local TTS, ffmpeg, requests, etc.)
- All file operations must use real file system operations
- All validation must use real validation logic
- All API integrations must use real API clients with proper error handling

### Testing Requirements
- Tests must use real file operations and real library calls by default
- Test doubles are allowed only at external-service boundaries or expensive orchestration seams
- Any mock, monkeypatch, or local stub must be explicit in the test name or surrounding comments
- External API tests must validate structure/logic locally unless clearly marked for live API access
- Integration tests that require external services must be clearly marked

### Code Quality
- Type hints for public functions and all new helpers
- Comprehensive docstrings
- Error handling with appropriate exceptions
- Modular, reusable code structure

### Documentation
- All documentation must emphasize real implementations
- Function signatures must document real method calls
- Examples must use real code, not mocked examples
